      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would like to append as well, that there should be an option to reset or retain the movement configurations.\n\nSay for example, I want \"Forward\" on the joystick to move my character forward in the direction of the head or hips, *but* **only** when movement begins. This means that the \"Forward\" direction depends on where I am looking when movement *begins,* as opposed to updating while moving.\n\nThe same can be applied to the other movement options (Hips, Playspace, etc), along with the option to use the calibrated directions (after doing avatar calibration of the trackers). In this way, the direction of \"Forwards\" will constantly be tied to the current orientation of the target, similar to how it works with the Head in live builds. Or optionally, using the orientation from the beginning of movement.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-17T03:05:34.967Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Add the ability to set the direction of movement of the player to lock to the controller or any available tracker / SteamVR device. This will allow users to have movement relative to their Hips for example, which helps people keep moving forward without slowing down or being disoriented when turning to look toward the side or behind, or relative to either of their controllers.",
